KB-277 C18b probe (the never-finalize stimulus lands loud AND routed).

This step is the never-finalize stimulus: it declares its schema'd `approved`
arm plus a declared fallback arm (no `outcome "default"`) that catches the
missing finalize BY NAME. Its session must produce NO submit_outcome call.
allow_tools is empty (no tools), so there is nothing else to do either — just
send a single short text turn now saying "C18b: this step never finalizes on
purpose" and then STOP. Keep doing nothing on every later turn.

When the turn budget exhausts without a finalize, the adapter's no-finalized-
result case is caught by the step's declared fallback arm and routes the step
to the failure terminal — loud AND routed (a committed StepOutcome carrying
the typed fallback name, the run ends on the failure terminal), never a
silent no-observation pass.

Do NOT call submit_outcome in this step, whatever happens.
